 stronger multilateral cooperation - ANI News", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "summary": "“BRICS must rally Global South”: Xi Jinping thanks PM Modi for hosting summit; pushes for stronger multilateral cooperationANI News", "published_at": "2026-09-13T09:31:00+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Asian News International", "tier": "international", "url": "https://aninews.in"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 65, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 12, "confidence": 0.15, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 25.0, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omission_score": 40.0, "headline_body_divergence": 0.0, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "b25345b4-ccff-4bae-9518-42ce0f509c36", "title": "What does this mean for #BRICS’ future?", "url": "https://www.news18.com/videos/india/what-does-this-mean-for-brics-future-10325190.html", "summary": "BRICS 2026: Prime Minister Narendra Modi has made a clear pitch for an inclusive BRICS, saying the grouping is “not against anybody” and will seek to take everyone forward.At the New Delhi summit, Modi called for a greater voice for the Global South in global decision-making and backed reforms to global governance institutions. He also proposed an emergency support network for seafarers, stressing the need for safe sea lanes and secure global trade amid ongoing conflicts.With BRICS now expanded and members divided on several geopolitical issues, what does Modi's message mean for the future direction of BRICS? Can the bloc become a stronger voice for the Global South while remaining an inclusive platform rather than an anti-Western alliance?Maswele Ralebona, Specialist News Researcher; Rahul Ahluwalia, Former OSD to VC NITI Aayog; and Ambassador Rajiv Dogra share their views.Watch the full discussion and the latest BRICS 2026 updates from New Delhi on CNN-News18. -News18 is your trus...", "published_at": "2026-09-12T10:39:25+00:00", "image_url": null, "sou